From: Oever Gonzalez <software@notengobattery.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt76: npu: make the rx descriptor chain walk memory-safe

mt76_npu_dequeue() walks a descriptor chain whose length it reads from
the ring-tail descriptor, with no upper bound: a stale or misparsed
count strides past the armed slots into entries with no valid buffer.
DONE stays set on a consumed descriptor until refill re-arms it, so
the walk passes the DONE check and either re-delivers already-consumed
pages or feeds a garbage address to dma_sync_single_for_cpu():

  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address ffffffff80000700
  CPU: 2 PID: 1472 Comm: napi/phy0-77 Tainted: G O 6.12.94
  pc : dcache_inval_poc+0x28/0x58
  Call trace:
   dcache_inval_poc+0x28/0x58
   __dma_sync_single_for_cpu+0xc0/0xe0
   mt76_npu_rx_queue_init+0x2ec/0x4c0 [mt76]  (static mt76_npu_dequeue)
   __napi_poll+0x34/0x180
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Oops: Fatal exception in interrupt

The mid-chain bail-out is also unsound: it frees the partial skb while
the unconsumed ring slots still reference its pages, and the same NAPI
pass's refill can re-arm those pages at the head - one page, two owners.

Make the walk memory-safe:
 - never walk more slots than are armed (clamp to q->queued);
 - verify the whole chain is DONE before touching any page;
 - order descriptor reads after the DONE checks (dma_rmb);
 - clear ctrl on consume so a stale slot can't pass DONE again before
   being re-armed.

A wrong count within the armed region can still mis-frame packets
(PKT_COUNT's layout is firmware-ABI-dependent); this change turns that
into a parse error instead of memory corruption.

---
--- a/npu.c
+++ b/npu.c
@@ -67,19 +67,27 @@ static struct sk_buff *mt76_npu_dequeue(
 	int i, nframes, index = q->tail;
 	struct sk_buff *skb = NULL;
 
+	if (!q->queued)
+		return NULL;
+
 	nframes = FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_PKT_COUNT_MASK, desc[index].info);
-	nframes = max_t(int, nframes, 1);
+	/* a chain can never span more slots than are armed */
+	nframes = clamp(nframes, 1, q->queued);
 
+	/* a partial chain can't be unwound: pages the ring still owns */
+	for (i = 0; i < nframes; i++) {
+		if (!FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK, desc[index].ctrl))
+			return NULL;
+		index = (index + 1) % q->ndesc;
+	}
+	dma_rmb();
+
+	index = q->tail;
 	for (i = 0; i < nframes; i++) {
 		struct mt76_queue_entry *e = &q->entry[index];
 		int len = FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_CUR_LEN_MASK,
 				    desc[index].ctrl);
 
-		if (!FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK, desc[index].ctrl)) {
-			dev_kfree_skb(skb);
-			return NULL;
-		}
-
 		dma_sync_single_for_cpu(dev->dma_dev, e->dma_addr[0],
 					e->dma_len[0],
 					page_pool_get_dma_dir(q->page_pool));
@@ -104,6 +112,8 @@ static struct sk_buff *mt76_npu_dequeue(
 		}
 
 		*info = desc[index].info;
+		/* a consumed slot must not look DONE until re-armed */
+		desc[index].ctrl = 0;
 		index = (index + 1) % q->ndesc;
 	}
 	q->tail = index;
